==Enemy==
A robotic version of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] piloted by a [[Doge]]. Universally amongst Teacher Bun Bun's variants, Mecha-Bun sports gargantuan health and DPS, but it also has an Omni Strike with 40 piercing range, with greater speed and attack rate.

Despite its name and appearance, Mecha-Bun isn't a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy.

==Strategy==
If you don't want Mecha-Bun to push, your safest option is to not let it attack at all. The best unit and the only one you will need to perma-freeze it in Eldritch Forces is [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]], who outranges Mecha-Bun's Omni Strike by 60. You might also want to use either [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] or [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] to stop Mecha-Bun in its tracks so your Necro-Dancer Cats can attack it more safely. The [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] can help with the beginning of the fight, as it will ensure that your crowd-controllers attack before Mecha-Bun. You also need some [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units to clear the peons such that they don't prevent your crowd-control units from hitting Mecha-Bun.

