==Trivia==
*Mecha-Bun's Japanese name contains the Greek letter Ω ([[wikipedia:Omega|omega]]), which is the twenty-fourth and last letter of the Greek alphabet and often used to denote the end, the final part, or the limit of something.
**This contrasts the final boss of [[Uncanny Legends]], [[Zero Luza]], who is associated with beginnings: its stage is named [[Revival of Origin]], its Japanese description states that it took in energy said to be the origin of all things, and [[Great Ape Luza]] is considered the origin of humans. Furthermore, [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|allied Mecha-Bun]]'s description refers to it as an ancient superweapon, while Zero Luza is an ancient guardian of the [[Sacred Forest]], and both enemy Mecha-Bun and Zero Luza have Omni Strike and attack with their fists.
*Its Japanese description directly mentions the [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] before the player first encounters them, whereas the English description describes it as an ancient empire.
*The "dark organization" in its Japanese description refers to the "organization conducting research to awaken ancient power" from the Japanese [[Stories of Legend]] ending. In [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], these were localized as "a dark union of [[Doge]]s" and "a shadowy conspiracy researching how to awaken Relic powers" respectively.
*Since Mecha-Bun consists of a Doge and a mechanical [[Teacher Bun Bun]], it can be seen as a combination of the first and last enemies from [[Empire of Cats]], as well as the last enemies from the two stages preceding [[Eldritch Forces]] ([[Twilight Zephyr]]'s Teacher Bun Bun and [[Unkept Promises]]' Doge).
*Not counting [[Idi:Re]], the first and last new enemies introduced in Stories of Legend are technological variants of the first and last bosses of Empire of Cats. [[Metal Hippoe]] is a cyborg [[Hippoe]], while Mecha-Bun is a mechanical Teacher Bun Bun.
*Prior to the [[Version 9.9 Update]], Mecha-Bun's Omni Strike had an effective range of -270~270.
*Even though Mecha-Bun is supposed to come as a surprise, the player can spoil its name for themselves through the ''Buns of Steel'' [[Meow Medals|Meow Medal]]'s description, which becomes visible after unlocking [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]].

